---
/** @fileoverview Renders an illustrative agent conversation about applying engineering rules before writing code. */
---
<figure id="agent-preview" class="agent-preview" aria-label="Placeholder agent conversation">
  <div class="window-bar"><span class="window-dots" aria-hidden="true">● ● ●</span><span>Agent / library-licenses.ts</span><span class="mockup-label">Placeholder</span></div>
  <div class="conversation">
    <div class="user-message"><span class="speaker">YOU</span><p>Write functions that collect a library’s license and notice files.</p></div>
    <div class="agent-message"><span class="speaker">AGENT</span><p>I found the relevant engineering rules. I’ll use them to write these functions:</p>
      <ul class="found-rules">
        <li><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><strong>Keep functions focused</strong><span>Separate manifest parsing, path validation, and file checks.</span></div></li>
        <li><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><strong>Use names that explain intent</strong><span>Make each step readable at the call site.</span></div></li>
        <li><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><strong>Document the contract</strong><span>State what comes back and when the function throws.</span></div></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="agent-close">I’ll compose those helpers into <code>collectLibraryLicensePaths</code>, then check the implementation against the rules.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption><span>Illustrative conversation, shown as a placeholder screenshot.</span><a href="#code-example">See the code before and after <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .agent-preview { scroll-margin-top: 5rem; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 56rem; border: 1px solid var(--cr-line); border-radius: 16px; background: var(--cr-paper); overflow: hidden; box-shadow: 0 12px 40px #00000006; }
  .window-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .8rem; padding: 1rem 1.5rem; background: var(--cr-surface); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--cr-faint); color: var(--cr-muted); font: .75rem var(--cr-font-mono); }
  .window-dots { letter-spacing: .15em; opacity: .5; }
  .mockup-label { margin-left: auto; font: .7rem var(--sl-font); }
  .conversation { padding: 2rem 2.5rem; font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--cr-ink); }
  .speaker { font-size: .65rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .13em; color: var(--cr-muted); }
  .conversation p { margin: .5rem 0 0; }
  .user-message { padding: 1rem 1.25rem; background: var(--cr-surface); border-radius: 12px; margin: 0 0 1.75rem 3rem; }
  .agent-message { padding-right: 1rem; }
  .found-rules { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 1.25rem 0; display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
  .found-rules li { display: flex; gap: .85rem; }
  .found-rules strong { display: block; font-size: .875rem; font-weight: 550; }
  .found-rules div > span { display: block; font-size: .825rem; color: var(--cr-muted); }
  .agent-close code { font: .8rem var(--cr-font-mono); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  figcaption { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .75rem; padding: 1rem 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--cr-faint); color: var(--cr-muted); font-size: .75rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  figcaption a { color: var(--cr-ink); text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  @media (max-width: 540px) { .conversation { padding: 1.25rem; } .user-message { margin-left: 1rem; } .agent-message { padding-right: 0; } .window-bar { padding: 1rem; gap: .5rem; } .window-dots { display: none; } }
</style>
